{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 180,
    "dDurationMs": 3105,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- This is the scariest chart\nin electrical engineering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 3285,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Puts the fear of God into\nall undergraduate students."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5905,
    "dDurationMs": 2204,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- First time that you ever\nlaid eyes on this chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8109,
    "dDurationMs": 1586,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what was your first impression?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9695,
    "dDurationMs": 1694,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Holy....\n- It's like terrifying."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11389,
    "dDurationMs": 2561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- It looks almost like a wormhole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13950,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in some sci-fi movie."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15290,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I mean, on many versions,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 16400,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it literally says Black Magic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19400,
    "dDurationMs": 2409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for all the fear, it's everywhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21809,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Millions of copies have been printed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23619,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's built into the\nmost advanced software"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25529,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we have today. That's\nbecause this chart solves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28209,
    "dDurationMs": 1791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of the most paradoxical problems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30000,
    "dDurationMs": 1529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in electrical engineering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31529,
    "dDurationMs": 2041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we put it to the test.\n- This is crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33570,
    "dDurationMs": 2349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We're getting way more power transfer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35919,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even though we've cut the line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37369,
    "dDurationMs": 1738,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How does that make any sense?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39107,
    "dDurationMs": 1183,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(both laughing)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 40290,
    "dDurationMs": 1449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There've been some great YouTube videos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41739,
    "dDurationMs": 1301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explaining how to use it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43040,
    "dDurationMs": 1789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like one from my friend Zach Star,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44829,
    "dDurationMs": 1990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but I always felt like"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46819,
    "dDurationMs": 320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were missing something essential."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47139,
    "dDurationMs": 2716,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You also, you wanna know\nwhy this chart looks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49855,
    "dDurationMs": 915,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the way it does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50770,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51603,
    "dDurationMs": 1566,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But then I need to know the physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53169,
    "dDurationMs": 2271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would wanna know what the circles are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55440,
    "dDurationMs": 1699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what I'm looking at at first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57139,
    "dDurationMs": 1931,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Because even once you\nknow how to use this chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59070,
    "dDurationMs": 1289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're still left wondering"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60359,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how it pulls off its\nstrangest bit of witchcraft:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63349,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trapping infinity inside a finite circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66689,
    "dDurationMs": 2601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, to understand that,\nwe have to go back 100 years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69290,
    "dDurationMs": 2364,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the origins of this chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71654,
    "dDurationMs": 1485,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1928, Philip H. Smith,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73139,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fresh out of electrical\nengineering school,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74869,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "got his first job at Bell Labs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77199,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The telephone industry was booming."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79239,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Americans were placing more\nthan 65 million calls a day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82639,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because telephone calls had\nto go through copper cables,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85619,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every call had a limit: the coast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88869,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the time, no telephone\ncables crossed the Atlantic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91579,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the only way to call across continents"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 93589,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was by using radio waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95989,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Smith began work on a\nmission to send radio signals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98269,
    "dDurationMs": 1701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from New Jersey to receiving stations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99970,
    "dDurationMs": 1879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands of kilometers away,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101849,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one in England and one in Argentina."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105369,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With only one antenna,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107459,
    "dDurationMs": 890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the signal radiates across the whole sky,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108349,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and only a small portion of\nthe power reaches the receiver."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 111399,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But with two antennas, the waves combine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113829,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In some directions, they\ncancel each other out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115599,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in others, they reinforce."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117379,
    "dDurationMs": 2371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So right here in the\nmiddle, the power doubles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119750,
    "dDurationMs": 1239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you add even more antennas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 120989,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it narrows the beam further."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122489,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Focus it to about 10 degrees across,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124619,
    "dDurationMs": 3311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the power in that direction\nis 400 times stronger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 127930,
    "dDurationMs": 1379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to have any chance of their signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129309,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reaching across the globe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130589,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Smith's team connected more\nthan 20 smaller antennas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133069,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a massive directional array"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135029,
    "dDurationMs": 2831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "linked by over two kilometers\nof transmission line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137860,
    "dDurationMs": 2179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Smith's job was to test\nthis massive array,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140039,
    "dDurationMs": 1861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but when he tried sending\na signal from the source"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 141900,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down the line to an antenna,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143580,
    "dDurationMs": 2289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, he noticed something strange."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145869,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of it was bouncing back,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147929,
    "dDurationMs": 2401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that reflection meant that\na large portion of the power"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150330,
    "dDurationMs": 1879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "never reached the antenna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152209,
    "dDurationMs": 1981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If he wanted to send a\nsignal across the planet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154190,
    "dDurationMs": 2459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he needed to make sure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156649,
    "dDurationMs": 1170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that all the power reached\nthe emitting antennas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157819,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So he needed to find a way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159029,
    "dDurationMs": 1591,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to minimize the reflections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160620,
    "dDurationMs": 1669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 162289,
    "dDurationMs": 2071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the reason Smith was\ngetting these reflections"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164360,
    "dDurationMs": 1849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that he wasn't working\nwith the kind of electricity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166209,
    "dDurationMs": 1214,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we might be used to,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167423,
    "dDurationMs": 1926,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like with a battery and a light bulb."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169349,
    "dDurationMs": 2261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here, the battery provides\na constant voltage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 171610,
    "dDurationMs": 1729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which drives a steady\ncurrent through the wire,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173339,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which lights up the bulb.\nThis is direct current, or DC."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176959,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But to generate radio signals,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178459,
    "dDurationMs": 2081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electrons have to oscillate back and forth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180540,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at radio frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 181950,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As they accelerate,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184360,
    "dDurationMs": 380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they create changing\nelectromagnetic fields"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184740,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that propagate out as radio waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187510,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the voltage has to rise and fall"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189660,
    "dDurationMs": 1389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and reverse direction,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191049,
    "dDurationMs": 1901,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the current has to as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 192950,
    "dDurationMs": 2650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's alternating current, or AC."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195600,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the simplest case,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197660,
    "dDurationMs": 1919,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "both the voltage and the\ncurrent are smooth sine waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199579,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, in reality, it does\nget a bit more complicated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201689,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than that, but for now,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203119,
    "dDurationMs": 2971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's just look at a single\nsinusoidal voltage and current."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206090,
    "dDurationMs": 1279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's recreate Smith's signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207369,
    "dDurationMs": 2133,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by shaking a slinky up and down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209502,
    "dDurationMs": 1268,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210770,
    "dDurationMs": 2266,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can think of my arm\nas the power source."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213036,
    "dDurationMs": 1234,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214270,
    "dDurationMs": 1969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So waves travel down the\nline to the other end,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216239,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you can see that they\nhave some key characteristics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218439,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The distance from one peak to another"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220149,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or from one valley to\nanother is consistent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222629,
    "dDurationMs": 1391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the wavelength,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224020,
    "dDurationMs": 2210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how many peaks pass a point per second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226230,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is the frequency of the wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 228250,
    "dDurationMs": 2129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if you know the number\nof peaks that go by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230379,
    "dDurationMs": 2141,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you know the distance\nbetween those peaks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232520,
    "dDurationMs": 1519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, by multiplying the two together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234039,
    "dDurationMs": 1891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get the speed of the wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235930,
    "dDurationMs": 1489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The formula is that the speed is equal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237419,
    "dDurationMs": 2171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the wavelength times the frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239590,
    "dDurationMs": 2299,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In Smith's case, he needed\nto emit radio waves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241889,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they sit on the\nelectromagnetic spectrum,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 243909,
    "dDurationMs": 3131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alongside microwaves,\ninfrared, and visible light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247040,
    "dDurationMs": 1229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And light waves all travel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248269,
    "dDurationMs": 1451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the same speed in a vacuum,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 249720,
    "dDurationMs": 3439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 300 million meters per second, or c."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 253159,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the transmission line,\nthe wave travels more slowly,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255549,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but for a given line,\nthat speed is still fixed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258229,
    "dDurationMs": 1561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if the speed is fixed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259790,
    "dDurationMs": 1259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, that means that frequency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 261049,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "must be inversely\nproportional to wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264059,
    "dDurationMs": 1341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me show you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265400,
    "dDurationMs": 1758,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(slinky clattering)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267158,
    "dDurationMs": 4441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you decrease the frequency,\nthe wavelength gets longer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271599,
    "dDurationMs": 2850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you increase it, the\nwavelength gets shorter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275389,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this wavelength is\ncrucial to our problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279019,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We'll also show you in simulation here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280599,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "without the effects of\nfriction and damping."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282869,
    "dDurationMs": 1940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, if we start out\nwith a long wavelength,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284809,
    "dDurationMs": 1881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the signal barely changes during the time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286690,
    "dDurationMs": 2049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it takes to travel down the slinky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 288739,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Once the wave reaches the other fixed end,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 290699,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "any reflection that comes back"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292129,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looks almost identical\nto the original wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295000,
    "dDurationMs": 1699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The resulting interference\nof these two waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296699,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't change the overall\nshape of the original signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299129,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all that much, so there's\nnothing to worry about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302009,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when I increase the\nfrequency to the point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304439,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where the wave becomes shorter\nthan the slinky itself,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307009,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, now when the wave\nreaches the fixed end,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309119,
    "dDurationMs": 2541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the reflection back interferes\nwith the incoming wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311660,
    "dDurationMs": 2729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314389,
    "dDurationMs": 1030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After a reflection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315419,
    "dDurationMs": 1861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the forward and reflected waves combine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318860,
    "dDurationMs": 1759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At some points, the two waves cancel"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320619,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the voltage is very small,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323179,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at other points they add together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325279,
    "dDurationMs": 3541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what's called a\nstanding wave pattern."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 328820,
    "dDurationMs": 3159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(slinky clattering)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331979,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In electrical systems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333069,
    "dDurationMs": 2541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the standing wave pattern\ncan be a big problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335610,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because if the reflections\nin your transmission line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337779,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are bad enough,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339589,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the peak voltages can reach\nup to twice the input voltage."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341709,
    "dDurationMs": 1350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if your line isn't rated for that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343059,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, it burns out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345029,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There was a huge reflection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346929,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a powerful standing wave did this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349649,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the inner conductor of\nthat transmission line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353759,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the effect of the standing wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 356099,
    "dDurationMs": 1417,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not made up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358460,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- In most electrical\nsystems we're used to,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360240,
    "dDurationMs": 1650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this isn't too much of a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 361890,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your house supplies AC\npower at a frequency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363980,
    "dDurationMs": 1810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 50 or 60 hertz,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365790,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that corresponds to a wavelength"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367290,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of about 5 to 6,000 kilometers,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 369440,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is far longer than\nany wire that takes power"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371740,
    "dDurationMs": 1129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the station to your home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373730,
    "dDurationMs": 1889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But Smith was generating radio waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375619,
    "dDurationMs": 1611,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the megahertz range,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377230,
    "dDurationMs": 3069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at 10 megahertz, the\nwavelength is about 30 meters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380299,
    "dDurationMs": 1541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With the transmission\nline he was working on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381840,
    "dDurationMs": 1549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more than two kilometers long,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383389,
    "dDurationMs": 1941,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, that's many times the wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 385330,
    "dDurationMs": 2229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, reflections were significant."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387559,
    "dDurationMs": 2011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why we went to\nImperial College London's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 389570,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "screened radio frequency anechoic chamber,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 392020,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see if we could recreate\nwhat Smith was up against."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 394540,
    "dDurationMs": 2579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- As you can see, it's very\nsmall and very compact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397119,
    "dDurationMs": 2881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we can do a lot of\nantenna measurements in here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 400000,
    "dDurationMs": 4119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can do electromagnetic\ncompatibility measurements here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404119,
    "dDurationMs": 861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Here's the experiment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 404980,
    "dDurationMs": 1939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've got a power source\nsending a radio signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406919,
    "dDurationMs": 2407,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down a transmission line\nto an antenna array,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 409326,
    "dDurationMs": 1333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we put it in an anechoic chamber"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410659,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to reduce interference."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412839,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've got a receiving\nantenna at the other end,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413739,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is able to pick up the signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 415259,
    "dDurationMs": 1991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and tell us just how much\npower is actually making it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417250,
    "dDurationMs": 1589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to our antennas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418839,
    "dDurationMs": 2061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a scaled model of\nSmith's configuration."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420900,
    "dDurationMs": 1389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, based on our input power"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422289,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the distance between the antennas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424299,
    "dDurationMs": 3381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we expect a signal of\nabout negative 55 decibels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427680,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's not what we see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429849,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've lost half the power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 431479,
    "dDurationMs": 2921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're picking up around\nnegative 59 decibels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434400,
    "dDurationMs": 2399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because signal is measured\non a logarithmic scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436799,
    "dDurationMs": 1491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that four decibel drop means"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 438290,
    "dDurationMs": 1699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we've lost more than half the power,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441199,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly what was happening to Smith."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443379,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, let's find out what's stealing it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445309,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To do that, let's simplify\nthis like a true engineer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447639,
    "dDurationMs": 1431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can model the electrical signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449070,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as a simple sinusoidal\nvoltage and current source,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452320,
    "dDurationMs": 1589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we draw like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 453909,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Next is the transmission line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455159,
    "dDurationMs": 2911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It consists of two\nconductors that form a loop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458070,
    "dDurationMs": 1519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the far end is the antenna,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459589,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its exact design varies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 461029,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so for now we'll just\nrepresent it with a black box."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463709,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That gives us a very simple toy model"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465599,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with just three parts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466879,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can represent\nthese parts with slinkys."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469689,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, so far we've used just one slinky,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471619,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with one set of properties,\nto show how waves travel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474369,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the real setup is more than\njust the transmission line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477589,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since both the antenna\nand the transmission line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479699,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have their own electrical properties,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481209,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can model Smith's whole system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482699,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by tying two slinkys together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484679,
    "dDurationMs": 1825,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One for the transmission line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486504,
    "dDurationMs": 1415,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the other for the antenna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487919,
    "dDurationMs": 2521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First, we're gonna try two\nvery different slinkys."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490440,
    "dDurationMs": 1769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One with a high mass per unit length,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492209,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and one with a low mass per unit length."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494649,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's see what happens."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496699,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(slinky clattering)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 499639,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, when we send a pulse down the line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501729,
    "dDurationMs": 2321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it reaches the boundary\nbetween the two Slinkies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504050,
    "dDurationMs": 1825,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of the energy continues through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 505875,
    "dDurationMs": 3504,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509379,
    "dDurationMs": 2171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And part of it reflects back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 511550,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The severity of the reflection\nis captured by a ratio"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514170,
    "dDurationMs": 1609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called the reflection coefficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515779,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its magnitude is just the\nsize of the reflected wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518289,
    "dDurationMs": 1791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "divided by the forward wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520080,
    "dDurationMs": 2729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if the two slinkys have\nthe same mass per unit length,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522809,
    "dDurationMs": 2067,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the wave passes straight through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524876,
    "dDurationMs": 1973,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The reflection coefficient is then zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 526849,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when there's a big mismatch\nin mass per unit length,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528899,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we get large reflections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531089,
    "dDurationMs": 2241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when the properties match,\nthe reflections disappear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533330,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because how the\nwave actually travels"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 535300,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the slinky\ndepends on two properties:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537970,
    "dDurationMs": 2186,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how tightly the slinky is stretched,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 540156,
    "dDurationMs": 1754,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this mass per unit length."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 541910,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But since in this setup both\nslinkys are tied together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544320,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're under the same tension."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 545880,
    "dDurationMs": 2719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, then the only difference\nis their mass per unit length."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548599,
    "dDurationMs": 1391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If we can match this property,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 549990,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's like the discontinuity is gone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551590,
    "dDurationMs": 1319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's just one slinky again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 553969,
    "dDurationMs": 2121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might think Smith\ncould do the same thing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556090,
    "dDurationMs": 1039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except instead of matching slinkys,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 557129,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he had to match his transmission\nline to his antenna."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560209,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what electrical\nproperty could do that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 562849,
    "dDurationMs": 1911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the mass per unit length decides"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564760,
    "dDurationMs": 2589,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how easy it is for a wave to\ntravel through our slinky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 567349,
    "dDurationMs": 2191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So an analogous version\nfor our electrical system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569540,
    "dDurationMs": 1829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might just be its resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571369,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the higher the resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572709,
    "dDurationMs": 2111,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the harder it is for current to flow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574820,
    "dDurationMs": 1139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's Ohm's law."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575959,
    "dDurationMs": 2316,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The resistance is equal\nto the voltage divided"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 578275,
    "dDurationMs": 854,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the current."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 579129,
    "dDurationMs": 1891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if a voltage wave hits the boundary"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581020,
    "dDurationMs": 2059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between the transmission\nline and the antenna,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583079,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the resistance changes\nacross that boundary,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585629,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, the whole wave can't pass through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 587489,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some of it reflects,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588539,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just like what we saw with the slinkys."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590989,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indeed, in real life when we checked,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 592329,
    "dDurationMs": 1391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the resistances didn't match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 594640,
    "dDurationMs": 2389,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the antenna array is\nat 12.5 ohms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 597029,
    "dDurationMs": 2170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the transmission line is at 50."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 599199,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, what we're gonna do is we're gonna add"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600589,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this 37.5 ohm or 40 ohm resistor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603159,
    "dDurationMs": 1790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to try to bring it up so that they match,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604949,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we'll see what happens to the power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607669,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, what are we looking\nat? So now it's at..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609769,
    "dDurationMs": 1451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, that's, it hasn't helped us at all."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611220,
    "dDurationMs": 1729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's actually, yeah, we're half the power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612949,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Interesting. But why is that?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615939,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Resistors have a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618089,
    "dDurationMs": 2161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They work by taking power and\ndissipating it through heat,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620250,
    "dDurationMs": 1762,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so they're fundamentally lossy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622012,
    "dDurationMs": 1617,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that means by putting\nit in our system here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 623629,
    "dDurationMs": 2301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're gonna lose energy no matter what."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625930,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's another problem\nwith using resistors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627500,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's that real-life systems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 628790,
    "dDurationMs": 1229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "don't just have resistances."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630859,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take this disposable camera."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632939,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I turn on the flash,\nit takes a moment to charge."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 635779,
    "dDurationMs": 1621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can hear it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637400,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then when I take a picture"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 638650,
    "dDurationMs": 2539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(camera clicking)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641189,
    "dDurationMs": 2421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "releases all that energy at once."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 643610,
    "dDurationMs": 2089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because inside\nare two conductive plates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645699,
    "dDurationMs": 1411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "separated by a gap."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647110,
    "dDurationMs": 2809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I turn on the flash, I\napply a voltage across them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649919,
    "dDurationMs": 1081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and because they're not connected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651000,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a charge builds up on\neach side, storing energy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653860,
    "dDurationMs": 1219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This forms a capacitor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655079,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its ability to store charge\nis called its capacitance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658479,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I take the picture,\nthe circuit closes,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660409,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that stored energy\nis released all at once,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662729,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which produces the flash."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664309,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this isn't just in cameras."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666459,
    "dDurationMs": 1701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A transmission line has two conductors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668160,
    "dDurationMs": 3369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "held a distance apart, so it\nhas a capacitance as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 671529,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it uses alternating current,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673139,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so let's see what happens\nwhen we have a capacitor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 675029,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with an alternating current signal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 676879,
    "dDurationMs": 1341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so we're gonna make a chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678220,
    "dDurationMs": 2866,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and on the horizontal\naxis, I'm gonna draw time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681086,
    "dDurationMs": 2703,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(marker squeaking)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683789,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And on the vertical axis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686649,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'll just have magnitude of our wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689389,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so we'll start\nwith our voltage wave,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691129,
    "dDurationMs": 2291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which we'll just draw like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693420,
    "dDurationMs": 2999,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(marker squeaking)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696419,
    "dDurationMs": 1658,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we'll draw our current wave in red."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698077,
    "dDurationMs": 2917,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(marker squeaking)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702149,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the voltage rises, charge builds up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704429,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the peak voltage, that buildup stops,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 706629,
    "dDurationMs": 1841,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and since current is the flow of charge,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708470,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the charges stop\nmoving, at that point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710500,
    "dDurationMs": 2229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the current is zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 712729,
    "dDurationMs": 1751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, as the voltage falls,\nthe charge flows back,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714480,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's when the\ncurrent is the largest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716440,
    "dDurationMs": 1270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So unlike resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717710,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "voltage and current don't\npeak at the same time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720470,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since the horizontal axis is time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722190,
    "dDurationMs": 2449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this shows the current\npeaking before the voltage,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724639,
    "dDurationMs": 3191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "always by the same amount,\na quarter of a cycle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727830,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In other words, the voltage\nlags the current by 90 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732209,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there is another effect\nwe need to take into account."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 734920,
    "dDurationMs": 2109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because whenever a\ncurrent flows through a wire,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737029,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it creates a magnetic field,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739410,
    "dDurationMs": 1809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you coil that wire many times over,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741219,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the magnetic field from\neach loop adds together,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743619,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which makes the effect much stronger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 745639,
    "dDurationMs": 2270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why in circuits"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747909,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you might often see components\nthat look like this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 748969,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even on a straight wire,\nlike our transmission line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751849,
    "dDurationMs": 1921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these fields still exist,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753770,
    "dDurationMs": 2219,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they affect the way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755989,
    "dDurationMs": 871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that our current and voltage waves behave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756860,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A changing magnetic\nfield induces a voltage"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759250,
    "dDurationMs": 2281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that opposes any change in the current,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 761531,
    "dDurationMs": 1539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the faster you try\nto change that current,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763070,
    "dDurationMs": 1529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the more voltage pushes back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765529,
    "dDurationMs": 1160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the current is at zero,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 766689,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the slope of the curve is at its steepest,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768939,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the current is changing the fastest,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771389,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "therefore, the voltage is at its peak."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 773639,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Further along the cycle, the\ncurrent reaches its maximum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776619,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For just an instant, it\nhas stopped changing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778639,
    "dDurationMs": 1401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the slope is flat,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 780040,
    "dDurationMs": 2309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's when voltage drops to zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782349,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Past the peak, the current begins to fall,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784129,
    "dDurationMs": 1571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the voltage flips direction."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786699,
    "dDurationMs": 2881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So again, the voltage and\ncurrent peaks don't line up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 789580,
    "dDurationMs": 2979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The voltage leads the\ncurrent by 90 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792559,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that's why matching\nresistances alone wasn't enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795349,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in our demo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797029,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With resistance, we can only\ndescribe the relative size"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799159,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our voltage and current\nwaves, or the magnitude,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 802119,
    "dDurationMs": 2452,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it says nothing about their timing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804571,
    "dDurationMs": 2378,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Capacitance and inductance\nshift the current wave"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806949,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relative to the voltage wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808459,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That is, they shift the phase."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810229,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So a real match needs two\nthings to line up, not just one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813689,
    "dDurationMs": 2410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have to match the\nmagnitude and the phase."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817209,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, one common way to represent something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819119,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with both a magnitude and a phase"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820779,
    "dDurationMs": 1721,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is to use complex numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822500,
    "dDurationMs": 1739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They consist of two parts, a real part,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 824239,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "represented on the X-axis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 826579,
    "dDurationMs": 3421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and an imaginary part,\nrepresented on the Y-axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830000,
    "dDurationMs": 1269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the complex plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832119,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, because electrical engineers\nuse I to refer to current,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834729,
    "dDurationMs": 2150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're gonna refer to\nimaginary numbers with a j."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 838229,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just to shake things up even more,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 839849,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most electrical engineering\ntextbooks swap the order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842369,
    "dDurationMs": 3321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so instead of saying\nsomething like 3j, we have j3."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845690,
    "dDurationMs": 2429,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, a purely resistive\ncomponent changes the ratio"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 848119,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of voltage and current waves\nrelative to each other,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850399,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it doesn't shift their phase."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 852319,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So on this plane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854379,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pure resistance lies\nalong the horizontal axis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 855619,
    "dDurationMs": 1051,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where phase is zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857669,
    "dDurationMs": 1741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since we care about positive resistances,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 859410,
    "dDurationMs": 1609,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're only gonna look at\nthe right side of the plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862300,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, compare that to pure\ncapacitors and inductors."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 864840,
    "dDurationMs": 2079,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These components do shift\nthe phase of our waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 866919,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "relative to each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869109,
    "dDurationMs": 1370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Since an inductor causes\nvoltage to lead current"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870479,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by 90 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 872859,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we rotate it up plus 90\ndegrees on the vertical axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874819,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A capacitor causes voltage\nto lag current by 90 degrees,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877919,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we rotate it down to minus 90 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881839,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Put them together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883759,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this vertical axis\nis called reactance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 885479,
    "dDurationMs": 2771,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can now describe any\ncombination of resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888250,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capacitance, and inductance pretty easily"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 890450,
    "dDurationMs": 1410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on this two-dimensional plane"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891860,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as just a combination of a\nresistance value and a reactance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895840,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This combined quantity\nwe represent with Z."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 897960,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's called the impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900280,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, impedance is still defined"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901800,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the ratio of voltage to current."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 903780,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's Ohm's law for AC circuits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905900,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Z is equal to V over I."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908250,
    "dDurationMs": 2549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now its magnitude\ntells you the relative size"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 910799,
    "dDurationMs": 1531,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your current and voltage waves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 912330,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its angle tells you\nhow the phase has shifted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 914730,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a pretty great real life application"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916660,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of \"jmaginary\" numbers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 918090,
    "dDurationMs": 3269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So perhaps this is what\nSmith needed to match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921359,
    "dDurationMs": 1681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, in every transmission line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 923040,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a built-in impedance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924480,
    "dDurationMs": 2909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called its characteristic\nimpedance, or Z_0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 927389,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is just a fixed property of the line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 929169,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's kind of like mass per\nunit length with the Slinkies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932000,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, in most radio\nfrequency or RF systems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934700,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is designed to be 50\nohms of pure resistance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937980,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the value we need to match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940200,
    "dDurationMs": 1269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do that, and it's like we've made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 941469,
    "dDurationMs": 2371,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the two Slinkies\nidentical, no reflections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 944779,
    "dDurationMs": 1551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's suppose we measure\nthe impedance at the antenna"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946330,
    "dDurationMs": 2659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's 10-j30"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948989,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a pretty bad match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950469,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like having two Slinkies\nthat are quite different."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 952829,
    "dDurationMs": 2181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have to cancel out that -j30,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 955010,
    "dDurationMs": 3136,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we can do that by adding\na series inductor of +30,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958146,
    "dDurationMs": 2043,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the imaginary part drops to zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 960189,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, inductive and capacitive\nparts cancel each other out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963529,
    "dDurationMs": 3410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That leaves the real part,\n10 ohms, and we need 50."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 966939,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you might think just\nadd 40 ohms of resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 969449,
    "dDurationMs": 2481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but a resistor loses power through heat."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 971930,
    "dDurationMs": 1759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the very thing\nwe're trying to stop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 973689,
    "dDurationMs": 1991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what if the resistance were too high?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975680,
    "dDurationMs": 2949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can't add a negative\nresistance in a passive system."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 978629,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, how do you match a\nresistance without a resistor?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 981319,
    "dDurationMs": 1791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, the answer actually already lies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983110,
    "dDurationMs": 1989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the transmission line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 985099,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When part of a wave reflects,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 986189,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the line now carries two waves at once,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988019,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the forward one and the reflected one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 990639,
    "dDurationMs": 1521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At any point, the voltage you'd measure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992160,
    "dDurationMs": 1809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is now the two voltage\nwaves added together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995169,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the reflected current wave is flipped,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997899,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so wherever the voltage is reinforced,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 999799,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the current's canceled."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001869,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That means that the impedance,\nthe voltage over the current,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1004559,
    "dDurationMs": 1830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "isn't just one number anymore."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006389,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It changes as you move along the line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1008489,
    "dDurationMs": 1871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And if the impedance is changing anyway,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010360,
    "dDurationMs": 1579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, maybe there's a point on the line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1011939,
    "dDurationMs": 2101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where our resistance is matched."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1014040,
    "dDurationMs": 2259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All that we have to do\nthen is find that point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1016299,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then deal with the\nremaining imaginary part"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1018510,
    "dDurationMs": 1168,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1019678,
    "dDurationMs": 2891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can do that with a\nlossless capacitor or inductor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1022569,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no resistor needed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1024769,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At that point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1026069,
    "dDurationMs": 1270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the characteristic impedance\nof the line will be matched."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1027339,
    "dDurationMs": 1681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But how do you find that point?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1029919,
    "dDurationMs": 2131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, more than half a\ncentury before Smith,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1032050,
    "dDurationMs": 2739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oliver Heaviside had described\nhow voltage and current waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034789,
    "dDurationMs": 3321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "behave on transmission lines\nwith a set of equations."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1038110,
    "dDurationMs": 2199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But actually using them\nto eliminate reflections"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1040309,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was difficult. Calculating\nthe right values meant working"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1043289,
    "dDurationMs": 2675,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through long expressions\nwith a slide rule."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1045964,
    "dDurationMs": 1105,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(upbeat music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047069,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1930s, this was no\nlonger just an abstract problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1050429,
    "dDurationMs": 2481,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As political tensions\nrose across the globe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1052910,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ability to send clear\nsignals across oceans"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1055360,
    "dDurationMs": 2169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "became strategically important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1057529,
    "dDurationMs": 2301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It meant you could\ncoordinate ships, aircraft,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1059830,
    "dDurationMs": 1409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "entire supply networks,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061239,
    "dDurationMs": 3091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "activities crucial to waging war."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1064330,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So scientists in other\npowerful nations began"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1066690,
    "dDurationMs": 1889,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to take notice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068579,
    "dDurationMs": 1761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the Soviet Union,\nengineer Amiel Volpert"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1070340,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "began working on the\nsame problem as Smith."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073030,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in Japan, engineer\nTōsaku Mizuhashi did as well."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1076900,
    "dDurationMs": 2989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They all wanted the same thing,\na simple graphical system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079889,
    "dDurationMs": 2651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that would make matching\nimpedances quick and reliable."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1084150,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, when Philip Smith\ntried sending a signal"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086080,
    "dDurationMs": 1209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down his transmission line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1087289,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some of the energy didn't\nreach the other end."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1089369,
    "dDurationMs": 2801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It reflected, and it came\nbouncing straight back at him."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1092170,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the same thing happens\nwith your personal data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094840,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You put it online, meaning\nfor it to go to one place,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1097070,
    "dDurationMs": 2930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it ends up coming right\nback at you through scam calls,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1100000,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "phishing texts, and identity theft."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101770,
    "dDurationMs": 1529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know I once got a text from a person"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1103299,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who I thought was Derek asking\nme for some personal info."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106239,
    "dDurationMs": 2571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was in a rush, so I just\nsent it right over to him,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1108810,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and of course, that wasn't actually Derek."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1110610,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They just gathered info about me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1111970,
    "dDurationMs": 2379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then used it to\ntrick me into responding."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1114349,
    "dDurationMs": 1311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There's a whole business around this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115660,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people who grab your data and then sell it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1117500,
    "dDurationMs": 2379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the highest bidder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1119879,
    "dDurationMs": 790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there's no hope for an impedance match"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1120669,
    "dDurationMs": 2041,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to solve this problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1122710,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Fixing it means tracking\ndown hundreds of data brokers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1124320,
    "dDurationMs": 2549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then forcing each\none to delete your info."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126869,
    "dDurationMs": 2401,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But with today's sponsor,\nIncogni, you don't have to."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1129270,
    "dDurationMs": 2279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Incogni finds those brokers for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1131549,
    "dDurationMs": 1781,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They figure out who's holding your data,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133330,
    "dDurationMs": 2259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they send removal\nrequests to each one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135589,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You just make an account,\ntell them whose data to scrub,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1138159,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and you let them do the work."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1139739,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So far, they've filed 120 requests for me,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1142320,
    "dDurationMs": 2159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 115 have already been completed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1144479,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's roughly 86 hours\nthat I didn't have to spend"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1146939,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arguing with data brokers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148449,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two full work weeks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149849,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, brokers are one thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1151459,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What about that one\nspecific site that you know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153849,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has your info with your\naddress sitting right there?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1156430,
    "dDurationMs": 2279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, with Incogni's\ncustom removals feature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1158709,
    "dDurationMs": 1151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you point them at any site"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1159860,
    "dDurationMs": 1519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where your information is exposed,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161379,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then one of their privacy\nagents takes it down for you."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164699,
    "dDurationMs": 3411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you wanna try it, go\nto incogni.com/veritasium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1168110,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Click the link in the description"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1169290,
    "dDurationMs": 1939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or scan this QR code on screen,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171229,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and use code Veritasium for 60% off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173979,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the closest thing\nto an impedance match"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175829,
    "dDurationMs": 1741,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that you'll find for your personal data."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1177570,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The junk stops bouncing back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179290,
    "dDurationMs": 1519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So head to incogni.com/veritasium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1181909,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and use code Veritasium for 60% off."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1184389,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'd like to thank Incogni\nfor sponsoring this video."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1186809,
    "dDurationMs": 2390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, Smith, of course,\ndidn't have a shortcut."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1189199,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To stop his reflections,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1190489,
    "dDurationMs": 2301,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he had to build the solution himself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1192790,
    "dDurationMs": 2119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Smith started designing a chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1194909,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He started with the complex\nplane but with a small change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1198779,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most transmission lines today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1200199,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have a characteristic\nimpedance of 50 ohms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1202649,
    "dDurationMs": 2101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that value can change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204750,
    "dDurationMs": 1970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The 75-ohm line, for example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1206720,
    "dDurationMs": 1729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "needs a completely different match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208449,
    "dDurationMs": 2071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if Smith had just plotted raw values,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1210520,
    "dDurationMs": 1629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, then every system would need its"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212149,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "own chart with a different goal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1214660,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Instead, he divided everything"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1216110,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by the characteristic impedance\nof the line, Z_0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1218910,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This normalized the values"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1220290,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that everything was now dimensionless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1222930,
    "dDurationMs": 2459,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And now a value of one\nmeant a perfect match,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1225389,
    "dDurationMs": 2211,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whatever the line's actual\ncharacteristic impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1228610,
    "dDurationMs": 2099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But already there was a problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1230709,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, the values of real circuits"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1232419,
    "dDurationMs": 2521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can fall anywhere between two extremes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1234940,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A short circuit, where\ncurrent flows freely"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1237030,
    "dDurationMs": 2859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with almost no voltage,\nso impedance is zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1239889,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And an open circuit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1241399,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where there's a voltage but no current,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1243279,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so impedance is infinite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1244919,
    "dDurationMs": 1961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A real impedance can take on any value"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1246880,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "between these two extremes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1248450,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So to show everything,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1249540,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Smith's chart would also\nhave to be infinite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1252450,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not so practical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255030,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Smith then had a new problem\nto solve, a geometry problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257340,
    "dDurationMs": 2379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How to represent infinity\non a finite chart?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260710,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Smith realized he was\na bit out of his depth,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1262740,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so he called in the help\nof two of his colleagues"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1264830,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who specialized in mathematics,\nFerrell and McRae"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1268170,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and together they realized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269370,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they could use a powerful property"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270880,
    "dDurationMs": 1869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of complex numbers to address the problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274240,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To see how this works,\nwe'll follow an approach"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1276140,
    "dDurationMs": 2749,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "3Blue1Brown laid\nout in an excellent video"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1278889,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that I highly recommend you checking out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1281009,
    "dDurationMs": 2351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, if we multiply any complex number z"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1283360,
    "dDurationMs": 1989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by some constant like three,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1285349,
    "dDurationMs": 2131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everything scales by a factor of three."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1287480,
    "dDurationMs": 2999,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, multiplying by real numbers\nlets us scale our value."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1291419,
    "dDurationMs": 3450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What about multiplying by\nsomething imaginary, like j?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1294869,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, if we start with\none, multiply it by j,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1297239,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then you move to j, a 90-degree rotation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1300939,
    "dDurationMs": 1331,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Multiply by j again,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1302270,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by definition you get negative one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1305250,
    "dDurationMs": 1869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, and you get negative j."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1307119,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One more time and you're back at one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309259,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, multiplying by imaginary numbers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1311309,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lets us rotate our value."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1313889,
    "dDurationMs": 2511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In general, multiplying\nby any complex constant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1316400,
    "dDurationMs": 2669,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it scales and it rotates."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1320549,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, suppose instead of\nmultiplying by a constant,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1322919,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we try a more complicated\nfunction, like 1/z,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1327389,
    "dDurationMs": 1221,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we apply that transformation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1328610,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the entire complex plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330310,
    "dDurationMs": 1559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1331869,
    "dDurationMs": 1971,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now the lines curve and\nthe whole plane warps,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1333840,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and at first glance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1334980,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it seems like all geometric\nstructure is lost."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337430,
    "dDurationMs": 2849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But zoom in and you'll see\nthat at a small enough scale,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1340279,
    "dDurationMs": 2511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every tiny patch still looks square."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1342790,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This transformation\npreserves shapes and angles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1345040,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's called a conformal map."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1347000,
    "dDurationMs": 1899,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you'll notice that\nall the values in this map"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1348899,
    "dDurationMs": 1961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that used to stretch off to infinity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1350860,
    "dDurationMs": 2129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, they now fit in\nthe center of this chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1352989,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, it represents infinity\nin a finite space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1356470,
    "dDurationMs": 1979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And one over Z is just one example."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1358449,
    "dDurationMs": 2830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are other conformal maps\nthat warp the plane this way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1361279,
    "dDurationMs": 1471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's what Smith realized."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1362750,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you could find the\nright map for his problem,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1365070,
    "dDurationMs": 1599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then he could bend the impedance plane"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1366669,
    "dDurationMs": 1621,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into something far more useful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1368290,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "See, up 'til now, he'd\nbeen working in impedance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1370290,
    "dDurationMs": 1169,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it had two problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1372489,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It stretched off to infinity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1373869,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it wouldn't fit in one chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1375489,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it changed as you\nmoved along the line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1377399,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so there was no single value\nfor engineers to match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380399,
    "dDurationMs": 2011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But think back to those two waves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1382410,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and instead of dividing\nvoltage by current,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1384360,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "try dividing the forward\nwave by the reflected one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1387300,
    "dDurationMs": 2069,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That gives you the reflection coefficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1389369,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, on a lossless line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1390569,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the amplitude of our forward wave stays"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1392419,
    "dDurationMs": 1521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same size everywhere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1393940,
    "dDurationMs": 1470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, does the reflected wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1395410,
    "dDurationMs": 2170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the magnitude of our\nreflection coefficient"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1397580,
    "dDurationMs": 1489,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is constant along the line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1399069,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only thing that changes\nas you move is the phase."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401949,
    "dDurationMs": 2430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, the phase angle of\nthe reflection coefficient"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1404379,
    "dDurationMs": 1820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "picks out an impedance on the line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1406199,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The two quantities then\ncarry the same information."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1408479,
    "dDurationMs": 2601,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unlike impedance,\nit's a lot more tame."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1411080,
    "dDurationMs": 2339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because the\nreflected wave can at most"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1413419,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be the same size as the forward wave,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1415479,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the reflection coefficient\ncan never grow past one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1418559,
    "dDurationMs": 2950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you no longer have to deal\nwith this problem of infinity."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1421509,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's plot it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1423059,
    "dDurationMs": 1761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We start by plotting one vertical line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1424820,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the complex plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1426800,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is a line of constant resistance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1428960,
    "dDurationMs": 1370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now apply the transformation,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1431280,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that line becomes a circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1433700,
    "dDurationMs": 1819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's try another\nconstant resistance line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1436770,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, this line becomes a circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1439630,
    "dDurationMs": 2039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can do this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1441669,
    "dDurationMs": 1571,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for all positive constant\nresistance lines."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1443240,
    "dDurationMs": 3049,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What we get is this\nwhole family of circles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1446289,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At r=0, the\ncircle is the largest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1448519,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its diameter runs from negative one to one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1450769,
    "dDurationMs": 1881,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the reflection coefficient plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1452650,
    "dDurationMs": 1090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As we increase resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1453740,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the circles shrink and their\ncenters move to the right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1456430,
    "dDurationMs": 2439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At r=1, the circle\npasses through the center."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1458869,
    "dDurationMs": 2071,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's the match case,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1460940,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where our resistance equals\nour characteristic impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1463070,
    "dDurationMs": 2329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As r increases further,\ngoing off to infinity,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1465399,
    "dDurationMs": 2761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the circles get smaller and\ncluster towards the right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1468160,
    "dDurationMs": 1339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "approaching the point one, zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1470439,
    "dDurationMs": 2870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, let's do the same thing,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1473309,
    "dDurationMs": 500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but plot all the lines\nof constant reactance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1474250,
    "dDurationMs": 2869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are horizontal lines\non the complex plane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1477119,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For positive values,\nthese are inductances,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1479199,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they map to circles above the axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1481910,
    "dDurationMs": 2709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As reactance increases,\nthe circles shrink."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1484619,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For negative values,\nthese are capacitances,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1486639,
    "dDurationMs": 2431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they map to circles below the axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1489070,
    "dDurationMs": 1209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As reactance decreases,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1490279,
    "dDurationMs": 2121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get the same pattern mirrored below."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1492400,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When reactance equals zero,\nthe circle has infinite radius,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495320,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it appears as a straight line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1496680,
    "dDurationMs": 1659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "along the horizontal axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1498339,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can get rid of the left\nhalf of the impedance plane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1500389,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we're left with our final chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503070,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One family of circles\nnow tells you resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1505610,
    "dDurationMs": 1849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the other tells you reactance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1507459,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we can still easily read\neach point on the chart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1509739,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in terms of its impedance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1510949,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by just seeing where\nthese circles intersect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1513299,
    "dDurationMs": 2311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But because this is the\nreflection coefficient plane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1515610,
    "dDurationMs": 2809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every point also maps to\na reflection coefficient,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1518419,
    "dDurationMs": 2230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and how far it sits from the\ncenter tells you the reflection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1520649,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coefficient's magnitude."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1522669,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that's really the magic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524159,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every point now holds two things at once,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1526209,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an impedance and a reflection coefficient,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1528529,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as that reflection\ncoefficient rotates,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1530259,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it walks you along the line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1531889,
    "dDurationMs": 2770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cycling through every impedance\nyou'd actually measure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1534659,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And just like our 1/z example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1536339,
    "dDurationMs": 2411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those values can now be anything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1538750,
    "dDurationMs": 1849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Impedances that once ran off to infinity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1540599,
    "dDurationMs": 2370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now sit inside this single circle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1542969,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the entire infinite range\ncaptured on one finite chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1546939,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, Smith found the\ntransformation he needed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1549379,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the Smith Chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1552279,
    "dDurationMs": 2091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the first time,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1554370,
    "dDurationMs": 1005,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engineers had a practical way\nto analyze transmission lines,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1555375,
    "dDurationMs": 2544,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it opened up a whole\nnew way of solving problems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1557919,
    "dDurationMs": 1420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let me show you how."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1559339,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here it is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1560389,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've printed a massive chart\nto show you how it works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1563029,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're gonna start over here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564879,
    "dDurationMs": 1570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you walk along this horizontal line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1566449,
    "dDurationMs": 2271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're still moving along resistances."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1568720,
    "dDurationMs": 2849,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Above the line, you\nstill have inductances,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1571569,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and below the line you\nstill have capacitances."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1575269,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the whole chart fits in a circle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1576729,
    "dDurationMs": 2681,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with magnitude of one all the way around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1579410,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So that's our chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1581460,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now let's put it to work\nto help us with the line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1582580,
    "dDurationMs": 2409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we measured earlier, the one\nthat was losing half its power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1585860,
    "dDurationMs": 2339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the measurement in\nthe lab gave us 36 ohms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1588199,
    "dDurationMs": 2630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of real resistance and\n74 ohms of reactance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1590829,
    "dDurationMs": 1641,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we have to match that impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1592470,
    "dDurationMs": 1879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We divide by 50 ohms to normalize,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1594349,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that gives us a value\nof z equals 0.7 plus 1.5j."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1598259,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we start with the real\npart of our impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1600339,
    "dDurationMs": 2201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These circles get bigger\nalong the horizontal axis,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1602540,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so 0.7 is the circle right here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1606890,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now let's find the imaginary part."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1608450,
    "dDurationMs": 2649,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's positive, so it's above this axis."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1611099,
    "dDurationMs": 3061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I'll walk along this way,\nlooking at these circles here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1614160,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to see where they intersect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1616500,
    "dDurationMs": 1559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And once we find where\nit intersects with 1.5,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1618059,
    "dDurationMs": 1490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, that's our impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1619549,
    "dDurationMs": 1441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Finding any impedance on this chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1620990,
    "dDurationMs": 1869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we just go through the same process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1622859,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We just find where the\ntwo circles intersect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1625119,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, we know to eliminate reflections,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1626969,
    "dDurationMs": 2711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we need to match the impedance\nof the transmission line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1629680,
    "dDurationMs": 1939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that happens when\nthe resistance is one,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1631619,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it matches our reference impedance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1632909,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that reactance is then zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1634969,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's at the very center of our chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1637860,
    "dDurationMs": 1559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, on a reflection coefficient plane,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1639419,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's the point zero,\nzero, which makes sense."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1642129,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's when you have no reflection,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1643379,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so V_r has to be zero."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1645509,
    "dDurationMs": 2441,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so our goal is pretty clear."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1647950,
    "dDurationMs": 2339,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We need to move from our impedance here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1650289,
    "dDurationMs": 1541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the way to the center of the chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1652750,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we draw an arrow from\nthe center to our point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1655110,
    "dDurationMs": 2399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because this plane represents\nthe reflection coefficient,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1657509,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the length of that arrow\nis then the magnitude"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1659369,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of our reflection coefficient."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1661259,
    "dDurationMs": 2991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, the magnitude is 0.68,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1664250,
    "dDurationMs": 2039,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means that the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1666289,
    "dDurationMs": 2660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reflected wave is 0.68\ntimes the forward wave,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1668949,
    "dDurationMs": 1691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that's exactly what\nwe saw in the demo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1671760,
    "dDurationMs": 2479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We also know that as we move\nalong our transmission line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1674239,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because the same forward\nand reflected waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1676159,
    "dDurationMs": 2171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are interfering, the\nmagnitude of the reflection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1678330,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coefficient shouldn't change."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1680040,
    "dDurationMs": 2509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So if we keep the distance\nfrom the center fixed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1682549,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we rotate around it,\nwe can trace out a circle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1685559,
    "dDurationMs": 2170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then every point on\nthat circle corresponds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1687729,
    "dDurationMs": 2311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a different position along the line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1690040,
    "dDurationMs": 1790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because the standing wave pattern repeats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691830,
    "dDurationMs": 1179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every half wavelength,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1693009,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we know that a 360-degree\nrotation on the chart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1696009,
    "dDurationMs": 3230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "corresponds to moving half\na wavelength along the line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1699239,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we can use this to\nmake our life easier."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1702519,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In our example, we wanna move\nto the center of the chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1704439,
    "dDurationMs": 2811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and for that, we need a\nnormalized resistance of one."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1707250,
    "dDurationMs": 1479,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we want our point on this circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1709720,
    "dDurationMs": 2309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Lucky for us, there are\nalready two places on our line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1712029,
    "dDurationMs": 1805,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that match the resistance we want."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1713834,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1714667,
    "dDurationMs": 3612,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1718279,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1720529,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We can take advantage of\nthat by moving to that place"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1722549,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the line. To do that, just\nsee how far it is to rotate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1726349,
    "dDurationMs": 2081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, it's 12 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1728430,
    "dDurationMs": 2879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, since 360 degrees\nis half a wavelength,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1731309,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then 12 degrees here with\na signal of 1085 megahertz,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1734649,
    "dDurationMs": 2170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, that's 3.1 millimeters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1736819,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a bit close to where\nwe want to put the line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1738599,
    "dDurationMs": 2671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we're actually gonna go\nto the next available spot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1741270,
    "dDurationMs": 2599,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is over here. We\nmeasure it out on this plate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1743869,
    "dDurationMs": 1821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and lay it down in copper tape."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1745690,
    "dDurationMs": 1699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "28 millimeters of extra line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1748549,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I'm gonna say it's there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1750449,
    "dDurationMs": 1348,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is approximately correct."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1751797,
    "dDurationMs": 1703,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1753500,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nice."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1755300,
    "dDurationMs": 1619,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, perfect. Now all we have\nis this remaining reactance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1756919,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, it's on this circle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1758639,
    "dDurationMs": 2411,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's roughly -1.8."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1761050,
    "dDurationMs": 1466,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All that's left to do is cancel it out,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1762516,
    "dDurationMs": 1633,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like what we did before."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1764149,
    "dDurationMs": 3101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In this case, since it's\na negative capacitive 1.8,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1767250,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can just add a positive\ninductive element in series."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1770610,
    "dDurationMs": 1099,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The equation's pretty simple."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1771709,
    "dDurationMs": 3121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "1.8 equals omega L over Z_0."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1774830,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We rearrange and we get 13.2 nanohenries."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1777830,
    "dDurationMs": 2679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, we can try adding\nsomething like that in the lab."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1780509,
    "dDurationMs": 2201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we decided to start\nout with a smaller inductor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1782710,
    "dDurationMs": 2197,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just to test how we move."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1784907,
    "dDurationMs": 2033,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All right, yeah. Okay, so\nwhat you can, what you can see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1786940,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is we've moved along the\nconstant resistance circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1789830,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not quite enough,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1791150,
    "dDurationMs": 2125,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we have to actually up\nthe size of our inductor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1793275,
    "dDurationMs": 2045,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(machine buzzing)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1795320,
    "dDurationMs": 2149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now we add the inductance\nwe actually calculated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1799520,
    "dDurationMs": 1333,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And sure enough."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1802199,
    "dDurationMs": 1561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay.\n- Lo and behold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1803760,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There we go.\n- Not bad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1806617,
    "dDurationMs": 1210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- There we go, just like that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1807827,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, no reflections."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1808660,
    "dDurationMs": 1757,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- We did it.\n- We did it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1810417,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Let's go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1811250,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay. Come on, come on, brother."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1814040,
    "dDurationMs": 1710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Come on."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1815750,
    "dDurationMs": 559,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's fine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1816309,
    "dDurationMs": 790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1817099,
    "dDurationMs": 791,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Look at that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1817890,
    "dDurationMs": 499,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, and we're getting,\nand we're getting what?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1818389,
    "dDurationMs": 1561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, optimal power transfer now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1819950,
    "dDurationMs": 926,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah.\n- There we go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1820876,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- For sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1821709,
    "dDurationMs": 2081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Man, that's the highest\npower output we've seen."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1823790,
    "dDurationMs": 1059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I think so."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1824849,
    "dDurationMs": 980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- I do think this is important."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1825829,
    "dDurationMs": 3421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, we've verified that\nthis crazy map switch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1829250,
    "dDurationMs": 3639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the complex plane to the\nreflection coefficient plane"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1832889,
    "dDurationMs": 2471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leading to these insane appearing circles,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1835360,
    "dDurationMs": 1269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they actually mean something."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1836629,
    "dDurationMs": 2650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, in real life we've used\nit to increase the power."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1839279,
    "dDurationMs": 1250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Crazy.\n- It is crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1840529,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It is crazy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1841819,
    "dDurationMs": 1330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is cool."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1843149,
    "dDurationMs": 2470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This chart represented the\nwhole problem graphically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1845619,
    "dDurationMs": 2770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in a way radio engineers\ncould actually use,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1848389,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Smith wasn't alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1849909,
    "dDurationMs": 2530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1937, Smith finished his chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1852439,
    "dDurationMs": 1290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and almost simultaneously"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1853729,
    "dDurationMs": 2661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mizuhashi in Japan arrived\nat a similar representation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1856390,
    "dDurationMs": 1819,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that same year,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1858209,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Volpert in the Soviet Union in 1939."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1860919,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Three groups working independently"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1862659,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all converged on the\nsame elegant solution,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1864769,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it revealed a much better way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1866159,
    "dDurationMs": 1921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to solve the impedance matching problem,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1868080,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one that was rarely used before"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1869470,
    "dDurationMs": 2409,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it had been too\ndifficult to implement."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1871879,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the chart, an open circuit\nhas infinite resistance,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1875209,
    "dDurationMs": 1083,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it's here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1877400,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A short circuit is all\nthe way on the other side"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1879500,
    "dDurationMs": 3109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it has no resistance,\nso it's over here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1883889,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What you'll notice is both\nlie on this outer circle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1886470,
    "dDurationMs": 3369,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that makes sense. An open\nor a short absorbs nothing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1889839,
    "dDurationMs": 1670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every bit of the wave comes back,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1891509,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so it sits on this\nreflection coefficient circle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1893759,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of magnitude one, the\nbiggest reflection there is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1897159,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this rim works like every\nother circle on the chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1900399,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Moving along the line walks you around it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1902599,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one full lap every half wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1904669,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So start at a short or an\nopen, add a bit of line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1907399,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and look what you pass through."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1909009,
    "dDurationMs": 1753,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Every reactance there is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1910762,
    "dDurationMs": 2648,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What that means is that by\nadding a short or open circuit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1913410,
    "dDurationMs": 1110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with any length of line,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1914520,
    "dDurationMs": 1989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can make any reactance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1916509,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of adding an\ninductor or capacitor,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1918459,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we get the same effect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1919479,
    "dDurationMs": 1991,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by just using a length\nof transmission line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1921470,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we need to cancel out the\nimaginary part of negative 1.8."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1925099,
    "dDurationMs": 1981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the cable we're using is coaxial."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1927080,
    "dDurationMs": 1690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's really two conductors,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1928770,
    "dDurationMs": 1719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an inner wire and an outer shield"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1930489,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "held a precise distance apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1932339,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Normally it just runs to the antenna"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1933899,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "carrying the signal in a loop,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1935629,
    "dDurationMs": 3017,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we can splice in a side\nbranch of the same cable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1938646,
    "dDurationMs": 2883,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a bit of extra transmission\nline called a stub."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1941529,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We've connected one branch to\nthe inner cable of the stub,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1944110,
    "dDurationMs": 1709,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one branch to the outer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1945819,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since at the end of our stub"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1947209,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the inner wire and the outer shield"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1948709,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "aren't actually connected,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1949949,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this means we've created\na break in our circuit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1952369,
    "dDurationMs": 1631,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the Smith Chart, that means we know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1954000,
    "dDurationMs": 1739,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that the end of the stub lies here"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1955739,
    "dDurationMs": 2061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the open circuit position."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1957800,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the rest of the circuit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1960360,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It sees the impedance at\nthe input of the stub,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1962710,
    "dDurationMs": 1910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't see the far end directly.\nwhich is this connection point,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1964620,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that depends on how long the stub is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1967190,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Think of the stub as a little\ncove branching off a river."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1970230,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Water runs in, bounces off the back wall,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1972450,
    "dDurationMs": 2509,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and flows out again, and\nthe length of the cove"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1974959,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sets the timing of that returning water."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1977199,
    "dDurationMs": 2811,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Size the cove right and the\nwater flowing out pushes exactly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1980010,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you want it to. And that's\nwhat the stub's length does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1982900,
    "dDurationMs": 3059,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It sets the timing of the\nwave that reflects back."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1985959,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We want it to equal 1.8 positive."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1989049,
    "dDurationMs": 2061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we start at where the open circuit is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1991110,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and walk all the way around our chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1993060,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1996540,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we stop at 1.8."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1999450,
    "dDurationMs": 2319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we measure the angle,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2001769,
    "dDurationMs": 1751,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we see that that's about 302 degrees."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2003520,
    "dDurationMs": 2379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, now 302 divided by 360,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2005899,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that gives us how far along\nwe've been on the circle."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2008279,
    "dDurationMs": 1770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we know that one full circle turn"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2010049,
    "dDurationMs": 1701,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gives us half the wavelength."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2011750,
    "dDurationMs": 1539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We get 77 millimeters."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2013289,
    "dDurationMs": 1871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That should be the length of our stub."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2015160,
    "dDurationMs": 1579,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that's the shortest\nlength that works,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2016739,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but since the chart repeats\nevery half wavelength,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2018799,
    "dDurationMs": 2490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we could add another\nfull lap, 92 millimeters,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2021289,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and reach exactly the same reactance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2024470,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We're gonna start with the longer stub"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2025830,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then trim it down to\ntry and tune our match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2028580,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We haven't matched it yet,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2030440,
    "dDurationMs": 1640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so we're still, we still\nhave some of this reactance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2032080,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we have to cancel out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2034360,
    "dDurationMs": 909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Exactly, yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2035269,
    "dDurationMs": 790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And hopefully as we cut\nthis transmission line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2036059,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shorter and shorter,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2037799,
    "dDurationMs": 1330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we'll move through that point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2039129,
    "dDurationMs": 2780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- All right, so let's do it.\n- Let's do it. Let's do it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2041909,
    "dDurationMs": 1911,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You tell, tell me what's happening.\n- [Professor Stepan] Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2043820,
    "dDurationMs": 1549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's just like a little bit basically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2045369,
    "dDurationMs": 2417,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Henry] Like that might be..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2048809,
    "dDurationMs": 2290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- [Professor Stepan] Come on, gimme that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2051099,
    "dDurationMs": 1487,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Ooh, that's not too bad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2052586,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Yeah."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2053419,
    "dDurationMs": 3651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- All right, here's the last little bit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2057070,
    "dDurationMs": 2449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Ooh, that's not bad.\n- A good match."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2059519,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's a good match, okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2062089,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's awesome. It's actually so weird."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2064199,
    "dDurationMs": 2990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Literally by just changing\nthe length of this line here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2067189,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this stub, we've matched the impedance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2070099,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Insane."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2071649,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Look at it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2072649,
    "dDurationMs": 1630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We stopped every reflection on this line"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2074279,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with just a break in the circuit,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2076169,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a dangling piece of cable\nconnected to nothing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2078429,
    "dDurationMs": 1300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trimmed to the right length."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2079729,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because the stub is\njust more of the same cable,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2082709,
    "dDurationMs": 2770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fix is made of the\nthing that it's fixing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2085479,
    "dDurationMs": 2491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the series stub we've\nshown gets the idea across,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2087970,
    "dDurationMs": 1399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but you'd rarely build one this way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2089369,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because a series stub means\ncutting into your line."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2091789,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In practice, you'd rather\njust solder it in parallel,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2094229,
    "dDurationMs": 1750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that introduces a new problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2095979,
    "dDurationMs": 2450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In series, impedances\nadd together cleanly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2098429,
    "dDurationMs": 2910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In parallel they don't, but\none over impedance does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2101339,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's admittance."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2103779,
    "dDurationMs": 1191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only catch is that\nadmittance curves the other way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2104970,
    "dDurationMs": 3119,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on the Smith Chart, so engineers\nuse a flipped version of it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2108089,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "called the Admittance Smith Chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2109949,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Using this chart, matching\nstubs in parallel is easy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2113669,
    "dDurationMs": 1661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, what we've done today is basically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2115330,
    "dDurationMs": 1549,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what RF engineers do every day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2116879,
    "dDurationMs": 1850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They play a game trying\nto zigzag their way"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2118729,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the middle of the Smith Chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2121849,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But all these charts\nhave one big drawback."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2123729,
    "dDurationMs": 2021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They only work for a single frequency,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2125750,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but real world signals\naren't this perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2127610,
    "dDurationMs": 2159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The moment you turn them on\nor change them in any way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2129769,
    "dDurationMs": 2281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they spread across a range of frequencies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2132050,
    "dDurationMs": 2129,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are even radio techniques\nthat encode information"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2134179,
    "dDurationMs": 1523,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by changing the frequency."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2135702,
    "dDurationMs": 988,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, you've probably heard of them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2136690,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frequency modulation or FM radio."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2139730,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In practice then, the response of a system"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2141390,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't just map to a\nsingle point on a chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2143640,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather it traces out a curve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2145070,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "across its frequency range."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2146570,
    "dDurationMs": 2439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of matching one\npoint on a Smith Chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2149009,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you try to bring that curve\nas close to the center as"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2150969,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "possible over the range you care about."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2153059,
    "dDurationMs": 2861,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even then, the chart is still useful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2155920,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Philip Smith designed a chart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2157600,
    "dDurationMs": 2869,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could revolutionize\nhow radio engineers worked,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2160469,
    "dDurationMs": 2541,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but at first, no one really cared."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2163010,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It took about two years of\nslow responses and rejections"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2166100,
    "dDurationMs": 1249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from technical magazines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2167349,
    "dDurationMs": 3281,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before Electronics finally\npublished Smith's chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2170630,
    "dDurationMs": 1719,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Engineers already had their own methods,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2172349,
    "dDurationMs": 1950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and this one required"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2174299,
    "dDurationMs": 780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a completely different way of thinking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2175079,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At first, adoption was slow,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2177239,
    "dDurationMs": 1783,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but World War II changed everything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2179022,
    "dDurationMs": 2798,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(upbeat music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2181820,
    "dDurationMs": 1189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the battle for the Atlantic,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2183009,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "German U-boats were sinking Allied ships"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2185139,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faster than they could be replaced."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2187189,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At night or in bad weather,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2188669,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the predators were almost\nimpossible to find."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2191559,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the MIT Radiation Laboratory,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2193459,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scientists were building\nnew microwave radar systems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2196029,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that could detect\nsubmarines on the surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2198169,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "even in complete darkness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2200479,
    "dDurationMs": 1091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in the middle of a war,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2201570,
    "dDurationMs": 1809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you don't have time for trial and error."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2203379,
    "dDurationMs": 2750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You need a fast, reliable\nway to fix these systems."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2206129,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, Smith's chart was used constantly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2208209,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When the war ended,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2210729,
    "dDurationMs": 311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "those same engineers\ntook the chart with them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2211040,
    "dDurationMs": 2399,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out into industry, into the\nuniversities they'd work in,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2213439,
    "dDurationMs": 2381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the textbooks they'd go on to write."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2215820,
    "dDurationMs": 1729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Meanwhile, the other versions of the chart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2217549,
    "dDurationMs": 1270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Mizuhashi and Volpert"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2218819,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were used in Japan and\nthe Soviet Union locally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2221129,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but weren't spread as widely."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2223169,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's why today we refer to\nthis chart as the Smith Chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2226849,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, granted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2228809,
    "dDurationMs": 1511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engineers don't need to\nimpedance match by hand anymore."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2230320,
    "dDurationMs": 2117,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Computers can do it a lot faster."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2232437,
    "dDurationMs": 1863,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this chart is still\ntaught around the world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2234300,
    "dDurationMs": 1149,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in engineering classrooms,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2235449,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and many engineers still\nrely on it to this day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2238849,
    "dDurationMs": 1890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's because while a\ncomputer can tell you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2240739,
    "dDurationMs": 2330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the perfect match,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2243069,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it doesn't tell you what\nto try or why it works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2244799,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Smith Chart encodes that intuition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2246779,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And because of that,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2248959,
    "dDurationMs": 1831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it's still a popular visualization\ntool in modern software,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2250790,
    "dDurationMs": 1859,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it's used in almost\nall radio frequency"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2252649,
    "dDurationMs": 891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "measurement tools."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2253540,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- So historically, we\nwould get a Smith Chart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2256040,
    "dDurationMs": 1140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we'd use rulers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2257180,
    "dDurationMs": 2879,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we'd use protractors and compasses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2260059,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These days, we use a Smith Chart"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2262139,
    "dDurationMs": 2070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more like a back of the\nenvelope calculation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2264209,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where it's like a map."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2265649,
    "dDurationMs": 1711,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like if, if somebody asks you,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2267360,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how do you get to the\nnearest tube station?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2269440,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You'd say, well here's an envelope."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2272360,
    "dDurationMs": 2086,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You go down the street\nhere, turn left there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2274446,
    "dDurationMs": 1175,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "go further down there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2275621,
    "dDurationMs": 1539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in the same way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2277160,
    "dDurationMs": 2969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we use it to navigate from where we are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2280129,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to where we wanna be.\n- Sure."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2282839,
    "dDurationMs": 730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it gives you an intuition\nof what direction to go."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2283569,
    "dDurationMs": 1801,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- That's right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2285370,
    "dDurationMs": 829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2286199,
    "dDurationMs": 1161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before the Smith Chart,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2287360,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "engineers were stuck using\ncumbersome formulas and guessing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2289360,
    "dDurationMs": 2029,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It took a concerted\neffort by Philip Smith,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2291389,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tōsaku Mizuhashi, and Amiel Volpert"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2293629,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to make this complex world of\nreflections and standing waves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2296449,
    "dDurationMs": 1510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "easier to understand."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2297959,
    "dDurationMs": 3121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For me, it brings to mind\nMendeleev and the Periodice Table"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2301080,
    "dDurationMs": 2110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or Feynman and his diagrams."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2303190,
    "dDurationMs": 2250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Smith Chart is in that same vein."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2305440,
    "dDurationMs": 1530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, much of scientific progress"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2306970,
    "dDurationMs": 1759,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comes not from new discoveries"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2308729,
    "dDurationMs": 2310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but from new forms of representation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2311039,
    "dDurationMs": 2181,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They make hard problems easier to solve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2313220,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and make further innovation\nand discovery possible."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2316040,
    "dDurationMs": 2820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Smith Chart helped advance\nradio frequency engineering."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2318860,
    "dDurationMs": 3370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was crucial in building\nmodern radar and sensing systems,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2322230,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the communication\nnetworks we rely on today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2324430,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were in no small part\nbuilt from this chart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2327230,
    "dDurationMs": 3391,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So yes, it's scary, but\nit's also damn useful."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2330621,
    "dDurationMs": 4338,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(light music)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2334959,
    "dDurationMs": 1821,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One last thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2336780,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Last year, we launched the\nofficial Veritasium board game,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2338580,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Elements of Truth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2341060,
    "dDurationMs": 780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a trivia game with over 800 questions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2341840,
    "dDurationMs": 1390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about science and technology,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2343230,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the twist is you don't just answer,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2345090,
    "dDurationMs": 2349,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you also have to put down\na number from one to 10"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2347439,
    "dDurationMs": 1671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for how confident you\nare that you're right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2349110,
    "dDurationMs": 1189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So you can know the answer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2350299,
    "dDurationMs": 2570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and still miss out on\npoints by doubting yourself,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2352869,
    "dDurationMs": 2311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which it turns out gets\npeople pretty fired up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2355180,
    "dDurationMs": 1009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our team is competitive,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2356189,
    "dDurationMs": 2421,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so every time we play,\nthings do get pretty heated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2358610,
    "dDurationMs": 1439,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The game comes out later this year,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2360049,
    "dDurationMs": 1050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you wanna pre-order,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2361099,
    "dDurationMs": 1151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a link in the description"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2362250,
    "dDurationMs": 2279,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that'll take you to the\nElements of Truth website."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2364529,
    "dDurationMs": 1381,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thank you for supporting this project,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2365910,
    "dDurationMs": 2917,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as always, thanks for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2372536,
    "dDurationMs": 833,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Before we go,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2373369,
    "dDurationMs": 2350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I wanted to thank Imperial\nCollege of London for having us,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2375719,
    "dDurationMs": 2351,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and especially Dr. Stepan\nLucyszyn and Ian Russock"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2378070,
    "dDurationMs": 1209,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for setting up the demo."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2379279,
    "dDurationMs": 2305,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as always, I wanted\nto thank you for watching."
    } ]
  }, {
